    "title": "JPS hosts Parent Engagement Summit with global theme - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Acie Lewis ,\n59 minutes ago\nJACKSON, Miss. ( WJTV ) – The Jackson Public School District (JPS) hosted its Parent Engagement Summit on November 12, 2025, in order to engage with student’s parents.\nMore than 60 vendors took part in the summit, which included various themes that involved different countries around the world.\n“We’re required to have parent informational meeting once a year, and so instead of just having a boring informational meeting, we decided to make it fun for our parents by giving them some experiences like the passport around the world,” said Erica Brown Gibson, with JPS Program Implementation.\nParents were able to receive critical information at the tables and were able to get their passports stamped. Organizers said this gives parents and teachers a chance to engage with one another face to face.\n“This is an opportunity for us to reach out to the community. The parents can see the different stakeholders at work with their children, as well as people in the community. We get a chance to see the students. We get a chance to see the families,” said Rhonda Hardy, a JPS teacher.\nClose Thanks for signing up!\nWatch for us in your inbox.\nSubscribe Now\nDaily News Copyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJTV.",
